050584 #edb/ref 1033 3724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050584 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "55af6a00-8e04-5e4c-9b3d-92389069bc63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Two-Variable Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1033 356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "59bac138-6475-51d1-971d-3bd216b92f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1031 "Simplifying Rational Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1033 68 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6ae775b6-8adc-58c2-abd8-8374a1314249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $5ky-13=7$ for the variable $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ddcd149b-a90b-5ed2-923d-75e8a84ff145" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $y.$ To do this, we first add $13$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ky-13 & =7 \\\\ 5ky-13+13 & =7+13 \\\\ 5ky & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $5k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ky & =20 \\\\ \\frac{5ky}{5k} & =\\frac{20}{5k} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5k}y}{\\cancel{5k}} & =\\frac{20}{5k} \\\\ y & =\\frac{20}{5k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4}{5k} \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\cancel{5}\\cdot 4}{\\cancel{5}k} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13902" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac 34 kx + 9 = 2$ for the variable $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6eb1b4ba-3182-5ecc-8ae0-72ec27036b29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}kx+9 & =2 \\\\ 4\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}kx+9) & =4\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3kx+36 & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first subtract $36$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3kx+36 & =8 \\\\ 3kx+36-36 & =8-36 \\\\ 3kx & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $3k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3kx & =-28 \\\\ \\frac{3kx}{3k} & =\\frac{-28}{3k} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3k}x}{\\cancel{3k}} & =\\frac{-28}{3k} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{28}{3k}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{1}{3} = -\\dfrac{ax}{5}$ for the variable $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b35596e5-5914-502f-87dd-89348ab1664c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =-\\frac{ax}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{-ax}{5} \\\\ 5\\cdot 1 & =3\\cdot (-ax) \\\\ 5 & =-3ax\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3a\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =-3ax \\\\ \\frac{5}{-3a} & =\\frac{-3ax}{-3a} \\\\ \\frac{5}{-3a} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-3a}x}{\\cancel{-3a}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3a} & =x \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{3a}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Equations With Unknown Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7c6535bf-7dd1-5231-a992-9aefb8066499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921861