62 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186487934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488162 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e9795343-ebe1-5a6d-9824-2c6e0c43c343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488180 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488180 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133663" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488180 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488180 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\frac{4}{3}=5vs,$ then $s=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488180 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06c556aa-e44d-528e-81fb-0f187fd8faf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488180 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} & =5vs \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} & =3\\cdot 5vs \\\\ 4 & =15vs\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $s.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $15v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =15vs \\\\ \\frac{4}{15v} & =\\frac{15vs}{15v} \\\\ \\frac{4}{15v} & =\\frac{\\cancel{15v}s}{\\cancel{15v}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{15v} & =s \\\\ s & =\\frac{4}{15v}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488184 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488184 #edb/ref 1069 "q-214556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488184 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488184 #edb/ref 1071 "If $2=-5ab,$ then $a=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488184 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b499b93-e0d8-519c-9fd8-51ac13674a1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488184 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $a.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $-5b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =-5ab \\\\ \\frac{2}{-5b} & =\\frac{-5ab}{-5b} \\\\ \\frac{2}{-5b} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-5b}a}{\\cancel{-5b}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5b} & =a \\\\ a & =-\\frac{2}{5b}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488204 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488204 #edb/ref 1069 "q-214615" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488204 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488204 #edb/ref 1071 "If $-\\frac{3xy}{10}=\\frac{1}{2},$ then $y=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488204 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c956651-7831-59be-948a-98c8e15c7d28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488204 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $y.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3xy}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{-3xy}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3xy) & =10\\cdot 1 \\\\ -6xy & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-6x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6xy & =10 \\\\ \\frac{-6xy}{-6x} & =\\frac{10}{-6x} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-6x}\\,y}{\\cancel{-6x}} & =\\frac{10}{-6x} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{10}{6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 5}{2\\cdot 3x} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3x} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488229 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133665" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488229 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488229 #edb/ref 1071 "If $2=\\frac{3}{10}hk,$ then $k=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76378346-6bd7-5f90-bb11-bc03bf523eef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488229 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{3}{10}hk \\\\ 10\\cdot 2 & =10\\cdot \\frac{3}{10}hk \\\\ 20 & =3hk\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $k.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $3h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20 & =3hk \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =\\frac{3hk}{3h} \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =\\frac{\\cancel{3h}k}{\\cancel{3h}} \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =k \\\\ k & =\\frac{20}{3h}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488234 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488234 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75488" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488234 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488234 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\frac{12nx}{2}=\\frac{4}{7},$ then $x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488234 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "821390a9-15de-5be4-b110-42ad4543a1a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488234 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12nx}{2} & =\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ 7\\cdot 12nx & =2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 84nx & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $84n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84nx & =8 \\\\ \\frac{84nx}{84n} & =\\frac{8}{84n} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{84n}x}{\\cancel{84n}} & =\\frac{8}{84n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{8}{84n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2}{4\\cdot 21n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 2}{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 21n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{21n}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488238 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488238 #edb/ref 1069 "q-214561" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488238 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488238 #edb/ref 1071 "If $5=-14ab-2,$ then $a=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488238 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8bf4f7f2-b45d-5aef-8d47-16e8d1e1f900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488238 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $a.$ To do this, we first add $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =-14ab-2 \\\\ 5+2 & =-14ab-2+2 \\\\ 7 & =-14ab\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-14b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =-14ab \\\\ \\frac{7}{-14b} & =\\frac{-14ab}{-14b} \\\\ \\frac{7}{-14b} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-14b}a}{\\cancel{-14b}} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{14b} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{7\\cdot 2b} & =a \\\\ -\\frac{\\cancel{7}}{\\cancel{7}\\cdot 2b} & =a \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2b} & =a \\\\ a & =-\\frac{1}{2b}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
